     ~130 PDFs, ~9MB. Proves the parse and gives one year of 在校學業 percentile

An exam that runs easy lifts every cutoff that year. On the same 1,139
departments, the mean 分發入學 cutoff moves 0.664 (108) to 0.551 (111) to 0.618
(114) — a swing wider than the gap between the 1st and 30th university, and
enough to reward whoever happens to admit in the generous years. Each year's
mean is subtracted before pooling, measured over departments admitting in every
year so that a changing mix of departments cannot pose as a change in
difficulty. 統測 is levelled separately, against its own years.
- This should be handled year-by-year. We should build an estimate of student percentile across the 2-4 test types we're using, then assign a final percentile to the admit track. Then when we pool across years, tracks, or departments we take a weighted average.
- Parameters shared across year and track in the bridging formula should be the only connection between years

 I'm only trying to finely discern the top 10% of students. The best tech school is 國立臺灣科技大學 at 17% and department is 嘉南藥理大學    藥學系 at 13%. We should rip out the tech machinery and just say "all these tech students are bad and compress the scale for uac". Then the only number we need is number of tech admits.
